# INVWINUA.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY: Admin > Users at
# level 3, the users in name order.  ENTER shows ADMIN in view mode.  INS
# shows a new user, with no status: a repetition that differs is refused
# in the dialog (MU_NOMATCH, the focus on the repetition), a password
# too short by the server, on the password, both then wiped; mended,
# TEMP is added at level 1, its group upper case.  CTRL-E on TEMP gives it
# level 2, and again status D, disabled.  TAB on the users does nothing,
# and ESC goes back to the list Users was chosen on, in the order and
# with the filter or scope it had: the item list by ID, then by
# location, the location tree, the overdue
# loans, the recent service list, a search's results, and the service
# records of the first item by location, whose ESC then opens the item
# list by location again.  Users chosen on the users keeps the location
# tree to go back to; after Browse locations from the users, ESC opens
# the item list.  The audit log, its filter empty, goes back by ESC as
# the users do: to the location tree, and to the users, whose ESC then
# opens the location tree.  The end by Exit.
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINUA.SNP is its snapshot.
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER ALT-A U
S USERS
K ENTER
S VIEW
K ENTER INS
S NEW
T TEMP
K TAB
T Temp User
K TAB
T lab
K TAB
T 1
K TAB
T Temp1986
K TAB
T Temp1987
K ENTER
S NOMATCH
K STAB
T ab
K TAB
T ab
K ENTER
S SHORT
T Temp1986
K TAB
T Temp1986
K ENTER
S ADDED
# from TEMP's status past the user name, the full name and the group
K END CTRL-E TAB TAB TAB TAB
T 2
K ENTER
S LEVEL2
K CTRL-E
T D
K ENTER
S DISABLED
K TAB
S NOTAB
K ESC
S ITEMS
K ALT-C R ALT-A U ESC
S BYLOC
K ALT-L B ALT-A U ESC
S TREE
K ALT-I O CPGDN CPGDN CPGDN CPGDN ALT-A U ESC
S OVERDUE
K ALT-I E ALT-A U ESC
S SERVICE
K ALT-S T
T IBM
K ENTER ALT-A U ESC
S FOUND
K ALT-I L ALT-C S ALT-A U ESC
S ITEMSVC
K ESC
S SVCBACK
K ALT-L B ALT-A U ALT-A U ESC
S LOCS
K ALT-A U ALT-L B ESC
S LEFT
K ALT-L B ALT-A A ENTER ESC
S AUDLOCS
K ALT-A U ALT-A A ENTER ESC
S AUDUSERS
K ESC
S AUDBACK
K ALT-F X
